    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "from dotenv import load_dotenv\n",
    "load_dotenv()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "6a3ba247",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Here’s a practical way to learn AI in 2026, whether you want to **understand it**, **build with it**, or **become an AI engineer/researcher**.\n",
      "\n",
      "## First: choose your goal\n",
      "AI is broad. Pick one:\n",
      "\n",
      "1. **AI user / builder**\n",
      "   - You want to use AI tools well, automate work, build small apps.\n",
      "   - Focus: prompting, APIs, workflows, no-code/low-code, product thinking.\n",
      "\n",
      "2. **AI engineer**\n",
      "   - You want to build AI products and systems.\n",
      "   - Focus: Python, ML basics, deep learning, LLM apps, deployment.\n",
      "\n",
      "3. **AI researcher**\n",
      "   - You want to create new models/methods.\n",
      "   - Focus: math, papers, experiments, PyTorch/JAX, training systems.\n",
      "\n",
      "Most people should start with **AI engineer** skills, then specialize.\n",
      "\n",
      "---\n",
      "\n",
      "## The core skills to learn\n",
      "\n",
      "### 1. Python\n",
      "You need this first if you want to build.\n",
      "\n",
      "Learn:\n",
      "- variables, loops, functions\n",
      "- classes\n",
      "- file handling\n",
      "- virtual environments\n",
      "- packages: `numpy`, `pandas`, `matplotlib`\n",
      "\n",
      "Target:\n",
      "- be able to write clean scripts\n",
      "- load data, transform it, plot it\n",
      "\n",
      "Good project:\n",
      "- analyze a CSV dataset and make charts\n",
      "\n",
      "---\n",
      "\n",
      "### 2. Math basics\n",
      "You do **not** need PhD-level math to start. But these matter:\n",
      "\n",
      "- **Linear algebra**: vectors, matrices, dot products\n",
      "- **Probability/statistics**: distributions, mean/variance, Bayes basics\n",
      "- **Calculus**: derivatives, gradients, chain rule\n",
      "- **Optimization**: gradient descent\n",
      "\n",
      "You mainly need enough math to understand:\n",
      "- how models learn\n",
      "- loss functions\n",
      "- embeddings\n",
      "- attention\n",
      "- evaluation metrics\n",
      "\n",
      "---\n",
      "\n",
      "### 3. Machine learning fundamentals\n",
      "Before going deep into LLMs, learn classic ML.\n",
      "\n",
      "Topics:\n",
      "- supervised vs unsupervised learning\n",
      "- train/validation/test split\n",
      "- overfitting and regularization\n",
      "- regression\n",
      "- classification\n",
      "- tree models\n",
      "- clustering\n",
      "- feature engineering\n",
      "- metrics: accuracy, precision, recall, F1, ROC-AUC\n",
      "\n",
      "Tools:\n",
      "- `scikit-learn`\n",
      "\n",
      "Project ideas:\n",
      "- spam classifier\n",
      "- customer churn predictor\n",
      "- recommendation prototype\n",
      "\n",
      "---\n",
      "\n",
      "### 4. Deep learning\n",
      "This is the bridge to modern AI.\n",
      "\n",
      "Learn:\n",
      "- neural networks\n",
      "- backpropagation\n",
      "- activation functions\n",
      "- CNNs\n",
      "- RNNs\n",
      "- transformers\n",
      "- embeddings\n",
      "- fine-tuning\n",
      "- inference vs training\n",
      "\n",
      "Framework:\n",
      "- **PyTorch** is the safest default in 2026\n",
      "\n",
      "Projects:\n",
      "- image classifier\n",
      "- text classifier\n",
      "- simple transformer implementation\n",
      "- fine-tune a small open model\n",
      "\n",
      "---\n",
      "\n",
      "### 5. LLMs and generative AI\n",
      "This is where most AI excitement is.\n",
      "\n",
      "Learn:\n",
      "- tokens and tokenization\n",
      "- transformers and attention\n",
      "- pretraining vs instruction tuning\n",
      "- embeddings and vector search\n",
      "- RAG\n",
      "- agents\n",
      "- tool use / function calling\n",
      "- evaluation and hallucinations\n",
      "- context windows\n",
      "- latency, cost, and safety\n",
      "\n",
      "Also learn the difference between:\n",
      "- using a model through an API\n",
      "- fine-tuning a model\n",
      "- serving an open-weight model\n",
      "- building workflows around models\n",
      "\n",
      "Projects:\n",
      "- document Q&A system\n",
      "- AI chatbot with memory\n",
      "- code assistant\n",
      "- AI workflow that uses search + tools + verification\n",
      "\n",
      "---\n",
      "\n",
      "### 6. Data engineering basics\n",
      "AI is only as good as its data.\n",
      "\n",
      "Learn:\n",
      "- collecting data\n",
      "- cleaning data\n",
      "- labeling data\n",
      "- chunking and indexing\n",
      "- data pipelines\n",
      "- SQL basics\n",
      "- vector databases\n",
      "- evaluation datasets\n",
      "\n",
      "Project:\n",
      "- build a mini RAG pipeline over PDFs or your notes\n",
      "\n",
      "---\n",
      "\n",
      "### 7. Deployment and product skills\n",
      "Knowing models is not enough. You need to ship.\n",
      "\n",
      "Learn:\n",
      "- APIs\n",
      "- FastAPI\n",
      "- Docker\n",
      "- cloud basics\n",
      "- model serving\n",
      "- monitoring\n",
      "- prompt/version management\n",
      "- experiment tracking\n",
      "- eval pipelines\n",
      "- user feedback loops\n",
      "\n",
      "Project:\n",
      "- deploy an AI app people can actually use\n",
      "\n",
      "---\n",
      "\n",
      "## The best learning path in 2026\n",
      "\n",
      "## Path A: beginner to AI builder in 3–6 months\n",
      "If you are starting from zero:\n",
      "\n",
      "### Month 1\n",
      "- Learn Python\n",
      "- Learn basic statistics\n",
      "- Build 2–3 small coding projects\n",
      "\n",
      "### Month 2\n",
      "- Learn machine learning with scikit-learn\n",
      "- Understand model training, metrics, overfitting\n",
      "- Build one prediction project\n",
      "\n",
      "### Month 3\n",
      "- Learn PyTorch and neural networks\n",
      "- Train simple deep learning models\n",
      "- Understand transformers at a high level\n",
      "\n",
      "### Month 4\n",
      "- Start LLM application development\n",
      "- Build:\n",
      "  - chatbot\n",
      "  - RAG app\n",
      "  - tool-calling assistant\n",
      "\n",
      "### Month 5\n",
      "- Learn deployment\n",
      "- Put one project online\n",
      "- Add logging, evaluation, feedback\n",
      "\n",
      "### Month 6\n",
      "- Pick a specialization:\n",
      "  - LLM apps\n",
      "  - computer vision\n",
      "  - speech\n",
      "  - recommender systems\n",
      "  - AI infra\n",
      "  - research\n",
      "\n",
      "---\n",
      "\n",
      "## Path B: for software engineers\n",
      "If you already code:\n",
      "\n",
      "1. Skip basic programming.\n",
      "2. Learn ML fundamentals quickly.\n",
      "3. Go straight into:\n",
      "   - PyTorch\n",
      "   - transformers\n",
      "   - LLM APIs\n",
      "   - RAG\n",
      "   - fine-tuning\n",
      "   - deployment\n",
      "4. Build 3 portfolio projects.\n",
      "\n",
      "This is probably the fastest route to an AI job.\n",
      "\n",
      "---\n",
      "\n",
      "## Path C: for future researchers\n",
      "If your goal is frontier AI research:\n",
      "\n",
      "Learn deeply:\n",
      "- linear algebra\n",
      "- probability\n",
      "- multivariable calculus\n",
      "- optimization\n",
      "- information theory\n",
      "- deep learning theory\n",
      "\n",
      "Then:\n",
      "- reproduce papers\n",
      "- implement models from scratch\n",
      "- study transformers, diffusion, RL, multimodal systems\n",
      "- learn distributed training\n",
      "- read papers every week\n",
      "- contribute to open-source research repos\n",
      "\n",
      "---\n",
      "\n",
      "## What to learn specifically in 2026\n",
      "In 2026, you should care about these areas:\n",
      "\n",
      "### 1. LLM application engineering\n",
      "Still one of the most practical skills.\n",
      "\n",
      "### 2. Agents and tool-using systems\n",
      "Not just chatbots—systems that plan, call tools, verify outputs, and complete tasks.\n",
      "\n",
      "### 3. Evaluation\n",
      "Very important. Lots of people can build demos; fewer can measure quality reliably.\n",
      "\n",
      "### 4. Small/open model deployment\n",
      "Running efficient models locally or on affordable infra is valuable.\n",
      "\n",
      "### 5. Multimodal AI\n",
      "Text + image + audio + video.\n",
      "\n",
      "### 6. AI safety, governance, and reliability\n",
      "Especially if you want serious roles in companies.\n",
      "\n",
      "### 7. Human-AI workflow design\n",
      "The winning products are often not “just model + prompt,” but smart workflow systems.\n",
      "\n",
      "---\n",
      "\n",
      "## A strong project portfolio\n",
      "A portfolio matters more than passive learning.\n",
      "\n",
      "Build these:\n",
      "\n",
      "1. **Classic ML project**\n",
      "   - e.g. predict house prices or churn\n",
      "\n",
      "2. **Deep learning project**\n",
      "   - e.g. image or text classification\n",
      "\n",
      "3. **RAG app**\n",
      "   - ask questions over documents with citations\n",
      "\n",
      "4. **Agent/tool-use app**\n",
      "   - assistant that uses calendar/search/database/API tools\n",
      "\n",
      "5. **Production project**\n",
      "   - deployed app with auth, logs, monitoring, evals\n",
      "\n",
      "6. **Optional advanced project**\n",
      "   - fine-tune a small model\n",
      "   - optimize inference\n",
      "   - multimodal app\n",
      "\n",
      "Put all of them on:\n",
      "- GitHub\n",
      "- a portfolio site\n",
      "- short demo videos\n",
      "- writeups explaining tradeoffs and lessons\n",
      "\n",
      "---\n",
      "\n",
      "## How to study effectively\n",
      "Don’t just watch courses.\n",
      "\n",
      "Use this loop:\n",
      "1. Learn a concept\n",
      "2. Implement it\n",
      "3. Break it\n",
      "4. Debug it\n",
      "5. Explain it publicly\n",
      "6. Build a project with it\n",
      "\n",
      "Best habits:\n",
      "- code every day\n",
      "- keep notes\n",
      "- recreate examples from memory\n",
      "- read documentation\n",
      "- join communities\n",
      "- participate in hackathons\n",
      "- write blog posts or threads\n",
      "\n",
      "---\n",
      "\n",
      "## Common mistakes\n",
      "Avoid these:\n",
      "\n",
      "- **Only learning prompting**\n",
      "  - useful, but too shallow by itself\n",
      "\n",
      "- **Skipping fundamentals**\n",
      "  - if you don’t know ML basics, LLM concepts are harder to reason about\n",
      "\n",
      "- **Only doing tutorials**\n",
      "  - tutorials create false confidence\n",
      "\n",
      "- **Ignoring evaluation**\n",
      "  - “it seems good” is not enough\n",
      "\n",
      "- **Trying to train giant models too early**\n",
      "  - start with small models and practical systems\n",
      "\n",
      "- **Not learning deployment**\n",
      "  - companies want shipped systems, not notebooks only\n",
      "\n",
      "---\n",
      "\n",
      "## Recommended stack in 2026\n",
      "A practical default stack:\n",
      "\n",
      "- **Language**: Python\n",
      "- **ML**: scikit-learn\n",
      "- **Deep learning**: PyTorch\n",
      "- **LLM ecosystem**: transformers, APIs, orchestration tools if needed\n",
      "- **Backend**: FastAPI\n",
      "- **Data**: pandas, SQL\n",
      "- **Deployment**: Docker, cloud platform\n",
      "- **Experiment/evals**: tracking and eval tools\n",
      "- **Frontend**: basic React or simple web UI tools\n",
      "\n",
      "---\n",
      "\n",
      "## How to know you’re job-ready\n",
      "You’re getting close when you can:\n",
      "\n",
      "- explain overfitting, gradient descent, attention, embeddings, and RAG clearly\n",
      "- train and evaluate a model yourself\n",
      "- build an AI app with tools or retrieval\n",
      "- deploy it for real users\n",
      "- debug bad outputs systematically\n",
      "- discuss latency, cost, accuracy, and safety tradeoffs\n",
      "- show 3–5 serious projects\n",
      "\n",
      "---\n",
      "\n",
      "## If you only have 10 hours a week\n",
      "Do this:\n",
      "\n",
      "### Weeks 1–4\n",
      "- Python basics\n",
      "- data handling\n",
      "- one mini project\n",
      "\n",
      "### Weeks 5–8\n",
      "- ML fundamentals with scikit-learn\n",
      "- one ML project\n",
      "\n",
      "### Weeks 9–12\n",
      "- PyTorch basics\n",
      "- neural nets and transformers overview\n",
      "\n",
      "### Weeks 13–16\n",
      "- build one LLM app\n",
      "- add RAG or tool use\n",
      "\n",
      "### Weeks 17–20\n",
      "- deploy it\n",
      "- improve evals and UX\n",
      "\n",
      "This is enough to get real momentum.\n",
      "\n",
      "---\n",
      "\n",
      "## A very simple roadmap\n",
      "If you want the shortest possible version:\n",
      "\n",
      "1. Learn Python\n",
      "2. Learn math basics\n",
      "3. Learn machine learning\n",
      "4. Learn deep learning with PyTorch\n",
      "5. Learn transformers and LLM apps\n",
      "6. Build projects\n",
      "7. Deploy them\n",
      "8. Learn evaluation and reliability\n",
      "9. Specialize\n",
      "\n",
      "---\n",
      "\n",
      "## My strongest advice\n",
      "In 2026, the best way to learn AI is:\n",
      "\n",
      "- **learn fundamentals**\n",
      "- **build constantly**\n",
      "- **focus on real use cases**\n",
      "- **learn evaluation**\n",
      "- **ship projects**\n",
      "- **specialize after you’ve built enough**\n",
      "\n",
      "If you want, I can also give you:\n",
      "1. a **6-month AI learning roadmap**,\n",
      "2. a **beginner-friendly list of resources**, or\n",
      "3. a **job-focused roadmap for becoming an AI engineer**.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
